+# Tool input validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+The registry enforces the JSON Schema supplied to providers before invoking a tool executor, allowing the model to correct malformed calls within the existing tool-round budget.
+
+## Contract
+
+- Invalid required fields, declared types and enum values produce a readable ToolResponse naming the property path and constraint, never an input value, without invoking the executor; logs likewise contain no input values, valid inputs including unknown keys pass through unchanged without coercion or defaults exactly once, and only an unknown tool name throws ([validated by: rejects malformed input safely and preserves accepted input](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L20)).
+- Static schemas compile during registration, an uncompilable schema throws an error naming the tool at that point, and execution reuses the compiled schema across calls ([validated by: compiles static schemas at registration and reuses them for ten calls](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L63)).
+- Function-valued definitions validate against the currently resolved schema each call, caching compilation by resolved schema object rather than tool name ([validated by: validates each dynamic definition and caches by schema object](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L88)).
